claim.claim-text:
a lever connected to a cam wheel through a drive gear having a plurality of drive gear teeth, wherein the lever has a first lever position, and moving the lever from the first lever position causes the cam wheel to rotate, and when the lever is moved through its full range of motion the lever is able to return to the first lever position without causing the cam wheel to rotate;
a first sled in a first sled position and engaged with the cam wheel, wherein rotation of the cam wheel moves the first sled from the first sled position; and
a first spring connected to the first sled, wherein movement of the first sled caused by rotation of the cam wheel loads energy into the first spring.
